Z||000000||fogglethorpe||08-24-2001||08:09 PM||||Out of seven dwarfs (ummm, sorry...make that<BR>"vertically unendowed". After all, I don't<BR>want the New York Times coming out with a story that says I hate shrimpy dudes).<BR>Anyway, out of seven dwarfs, I have found <BR>the one called "Sneezy" to be the most intriguing. So, I went to "findoutprivatestuffaboutotherpeople.com" and looked up his family history. Here are some of his relatives:<P>Cheezy- This one is a nightclub singer. His nightly encores include "Little things mean alot" and "Short people".(Hence the name "Cheezy")<P>Greezy- He is not known to have bathed since November 12, 1989, and that was accidental. (Long story)<P>Meezly- He is always broke, and hit the skids after being fired from his position as "Center" on the village basketball team.<P>Eezy- She is, to put it bluntly, the floozie of the family.<P>Uneezy- Eezy's twin brother; He is nervous, and constantly chewing raspberry Tums.<P>Queezy- He is sickly, and no fun in restaurants. He is infamous for an occurrence at Chez Louis, when he took on an aqua hue, and hurled profusely on the waiter's kneecaps.<P>Weezy- George Jefferson's wife, and half owner of the Upper East Side dry cleaning empire. At a comparatively statuesque 5'4", she is certainly no dwarf, but for some bizarre reason, worth a mention.<P>Sleezy- He has held a number of jobs, among them used auto sales, politics, televangelism, and injury lawyer. He currently has a daytime tv talk show.<P>Squeezy- He is the best looking, most athletic, and tallest of the family, at 4'2". It is rumored that he had a brief romance with the fair Snow White. The romance abruptly ended, however, when his other family members made fun of him by saying that when he and Snow danced, it looked like he had three heads.<P>   <P><P>------------------<BR>I don't think so;therefore, I'm probably not.||||reg||1
